UPDATE lessons SET title='Year 3, Week 11, Lesson 2: Division facts and the link to multiplication', data=json_patch(data,'{"child_mission":"Division facts link to multiplication: if 4×6=24, then 24÷6=4 and 24÷4=6. Fact families hold the same three numbers.","coming_soon":null,"duration_minutes":55,"evidence_instructions":"Save the independent response, specific revisions and both short-answer explanations; record oral evidence for speaking tasks.","explicit_teaching":null,"extension":"Apply the same method to a larger number or a new context, then compare two solution paths for accuracy.","follow_up_challenges":null,"guided_practice":"PRACTISE BEFORE READING THE FEEDBACK\nWrite the fact family for 5, 8 and 40.\n\nFEEDBACK\n5×8=40; 8×5=40; 40÷5=8; 40÷8=5.\n\nWATCH FOR\nTreating division as unrelated to multiplication makes missing facts harder to rebuild.","hoard_words":null,"independent_task":"INDEPENDENT EVIDENCE\nBuild ten multiplication/division fact families. For four of them write a division word sentence using sharing or grouping language.\n\nWrite a short reflection naming one step you corrected and why.","interactive_activities":null,"learning_area":"Mathematics","learning_intention":"Division facts link to multiplication: if 4×6=24, then 24÷6=4 and 24÷4=6. Fact families hold the same three numbers.","lesson_number":2,"lesson_role":"Strategies","materials":["Paper or typed answer space","Pencil","Optional: place-value chart or number line"],"offline_alternative":"Use paper and pencil to complete the original task, then retain a photograph or short parent observation as evidence.","outcome_codes":["MA2-MR-01"],"parent_notes":"Parent: Marking guidance for the independent task: Build ten multiplication/division fact families. For four of them write a division word sentence using sharing or grouping language. Accept equivalent original responses that show the same skill.\n\nParent: Written model 1: Original response on new material: 5×8=40; 8×5=40; 40÷5=8; 40÷8